      "side": 1,
      "message": "The filter only gets the advertised map, not the updates. So if it drops the ref being pushed, a plain fast-forward of `refs/heads/master` sends master\u0027s whole history. That old id is always the most useful have and costs just one entry. Should we always add the advertised id of each `RemoteRefUpdate`\u0027s remote ref here, whatever the filter returns? Callers could then filter aggressively (e.g. keep nothing) without that trap.\n\n```suggestion\n\t\t\tfor (RemoteRefUpdate r : refUpdates.values()) {\n\t\t\t\tif (!ObjectId.zeroId().equals(r.getNewObjectId()))\n\t\t\t\t\tnewObjects.add(r.getNewObjectId());\n\t\t\t\tRef adv \u003d getRef(r.getRemoteName());\n\t\t\t\tif (adv !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 adv.getObjectId() !\u003d null\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\u0026\u0026 local.getObjectDatabase().has(adv.getObjectId()))\n\t\t\t\t\tremoteObjects.add(adv.getObjectId());\n\t\t\t}\n```",
